u2013&nbsp;The Church and the Struggle&nbsp;<\\/h2>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>with&nbsp;Jennifer Scanlon, Genna Rae McNeil,&nbsp;Reverend&nbsp;William Barber,&nbsp;Reverend&nbsp;Raphael Warnock<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n<h2>May 5 \\u2013&nbsp;Educational Injustice and Organizing<\\/h2>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>with Matt Delmont, Ansley Erickson, Carla Shedd&nbsp;<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n<h2>June 2 \\u2013&nbsp;The Struggle against Racism and Repression<\\/h2>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>with Aram Goudsouzian, Aldon Morris and Caleb Smith<\\/p>\",\"33\":{\"343\":{\"type\":\"image\",\"enabled\":\"1\",\"fields\":{\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"imageasset\":[\"340\"]}},\"344\":{\"type\":\"image\",\"enabled\":\"1\",\"fields\":{\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"imageasset\":[\"339\"]}},\"345\":{\"type\":\"image\",\"enabled\":\"1\",\"fields\":{\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"imageasset\":[\"338\"]}}},\"3\":\"\"}}','2016-04-07 18:30:16','2016-04-07 18:30:16','0b6dae60-aa65-4a13-92a4-b7a1c8646c1e'),(460,350,3,1,'en_us',1,'','{\"typeId\":\"6\",\"authorId\":\"1\",\"title\":\"Spring 2016\",\"slug\":\"spring-2016\",\"postDate\":null,\"expiryDate\":null,\"enabled\":0,\"parentId\":\"\",\"fields\":{\"2\":\"\"}}','2016-06-13 18:28:00','2016-06-13 18:28:00','cb4f41af-ca43-4f4a-9cfd-c806fcb732e4'),(461,352,4,1,'en_us',1,'','{\"typeId\":null,\"authorId\":\"1\",\"title\":\"Rhonda Williams\",\"slug\":\"rhonda-williams\",\"postDate\":1465844311,\"expiryDate\":null,\"enabled\":1,\"parentId\":\"\",\"fields\":{\"7\":\"Case Western Reserve\",\"10\":\"\",\"9\":\"rhonda.williams@case.edu\",\"11\":\"http:\\/\\/history.case.edu\\/faculty\\/rhonda-williams\\/\",\"12\":[\"351\"],\"8\":\"\"}}','2016-06-13 18:58:31','2016-06-13 18:58:31','df1d0fda-a255-4d71-bf18-1559bdc0e528'),(462,354,4,1,'en_us',1,'','{\"typeId\":null,\"authorId\":\"1\",\"title\":\"Kenneth Janken\",\"slug\":\"kenneth-janken\",\"postDate\":1465844533,\"expiryDate\":null,\"enabled\":1,\"parentId\":\"\",\"fields\":{\"7\":\"University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill\",\"10\":\"\",\"9\":\"krjanken@email.unc.edu\",\"11\":\"http:\\/\\/aaad.unc.edu\\/faculty-staff\\/kenneth-janken\\/\",\"12\":[\"353\"],\"8\":\"\"}}','2016-06-13 19:02:13','2016-06-13 19:02:13','09d5cd3c-41ab-4466-8bb8-abaf553ad72a'),(463,356,4,1,'en_us',1,'','{\"typeId\":null,\"authorId\":\"1\",\"title\":\"Erik McDuffie\",\"slug\":\"erik-mcduffie\",\"postDate\":1465844766,\"expiryDate\":null,\"enabled\":1,\"parentId\":\"\",\"fields\":{\"7\":\"University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign\",\"10\":\"\",\"9\":\"emcduffi@illinois.edu\",\"11\":\"http:\\/\\/www.history.illinois.edu\\/people\\/emcduffi\",\"12\":[\"355\"],\"8\":\"ErikSMcDuffie\"}}','2016-06-13 19:06:06','2016-06-13 19:06:06','5d0eaa4a-1ec0-4f17-9a26-b7e732409459'),(464,360,3,1,'en_us',1,'','{\"typeId\":\"3\",\"authorId\":\"1\",\"title\":\"Black Power and Political Repression\",\"slug\":\"black-power-and-political-repression\",\"postDate\":1465844994,\"expiryDate\":null,\"enabled\":1,\"parentId\":\"350\",\"fields\":{\"13\":[\"359\",\"358\",\"357\"],\"5\":{\"date\":\"2\\/4\\/2016\"},\"18\":\"<p>This year marks the 50th&nbsp;anniversary of the Black Power slogan articulated by Stokely Carmichael, Willie Ricks and SNCC in June 1966. Black Power was marked by triumph and tragedy. The triumphs include imaginative Grassroots agendas and concrete demands for justice as well as persistent&nbsp;protests against racism and poverty; the tragedies include the assassination of Malcolm X and Dr. King, the Orangeburg Massacre and the unjust imprisonment of legions of organizers and leaders like North Carolina\\u2019s Wilmington Ten&mdash;among them Ben Chavis.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>Please join the conversation with Rhonda Williams, author of&nbsp;<i>Concrete Demands: The Search for Black Power in the 20th&nbsp;Century<\\/i>; Kenneth Janken, author of&nbsp;<i>The Wilmington Ten<\\/i>; and Erik McDuffie, author of&nbsp;<i>Sojourning for Freedom: Black Women, American Communism and the Making of Black Left Feminism<\\/i>&nbsp;and an important new biographical study of Malcolm X\\u2019s mother, Louise Langdon Little.<\\/p>\",\"19\":\"http:\\/\\/www.eventbrite.com\\/e\\/conversations-in-black-freedom-studies-black-power-and-radical-repression-tickets-20286580709\",\"24\":\"\",\"14\":[\"356\",\"352\",\"354\"],\"17\":\"\"}}','2016-06-13 19:09:54','2016-06-13 19:09:54','9c82d754-3661-41a6-9a0c-2371e3381f82'),(465,350,3,1,'en_us',2,'','{\"typeId\":\"6\",\"authorId\":\"1\",\"title\":\"Spring 2016\",\"slug\":\"spring-2016\",\"postDate\":1465845133,\"expiryDate\":null,\"enabled\":1,\"parentId\":\"\",\"fields\":{\"2\":\"\"}}','2016-06-13 19:12:13','2016-06-13 19:12:13','ee1f641d-a2b7-48cb-b886-c11115a26779'),(466,350,3,1,'en_us',3,'','{\"typeId\":\"6\",\"authorId\":\"1\",\"title\":\"Spring 2016\",\"slug\":\"spring-2016\",\"postDate\":1465845120,\"expiryDate\":null,\"enabled\":0,\"parentId\":\"\",\"fields\":{\"2\":\"\"}}','2016-06-13 19:14:41','2016-06-13 19:14:41','8c06a417-3582-47c1-8df4-febba3d6a573'),(467,360,3,1,'en_us',2,'','{\"typeId\":\"3\",\"authorId\":\"1\",\"title\":\"Black Power and Political Repression\",\"slug\":\"black-power-and-political-repression\",\"postDate\":1465844940,\"expiryDate\":null,\"enabled\":1,\"parentId\":\"350\",\"fields\":{\"13\":[\"359\",\"358\",\"357\"],\"5\":{\"date\":\"2\\/4\\/2016\"},\"18\":\"<p>This year marks the 50th&nbsp;anniversary of the Black Power slogan articulated by Stokely Carmichael, Willie Ricks and SNCC in June 1966. Black Power was marked by triumph and tragedy. The triumphs include imaginative Grassroots agendas and concrete demands for justice as well as persistent&nbsp;protests against racism and poverty; the tragedies include the assassination of Malcolm X and Dr. King, the Orangeburg Massacre and the unjust imprisonment of legions of organizers and leaders like North Carolina\\u2019s Wilmington Ten&mdash;among them Ben Chavis.<\\/p>\\r\\n\\r\\n<p>Please join the conversation with Rhonda Williams, author of&nbsp;<em>Concrete Demands: The Search for Black Power in the 20th&nbsp;Century<\\/em>; Kenneth Janken, author of&nbsp;<em>The Wilmington Ten<\\/em>; and Erik McDuffie, author of&nbsp;<em>Sojourning for Freedom: Black Women, American Communism and the Making of Black Left Feminism<\\/em>&nbsp;and an important new biographical study of Malcolm X\\u2019s mother, Louise Langdon Little.<\\/p>\",\"19\":\"http:\\/\\/www.eventbrite.com\\/e\\/conversations-in-black-freedom-studies-black-power-and-radical-repression-tickets-20286580709\",\"24\":\"\",\"14\":[\"356\",\"352\",\"354\"],\"17\":\"\"}}','2016-06-13 19:26:18','2016-06-13 19:26:18','9238741f-47c7-4ea4-b186-adc1c282c740'),(468,362,4,1,'en_us',1,NULL,'{\"typeId\":null,\"authorId\":\"1\",\"title\":\"Ericka Huggins\",\"slug\":\"ericka-huggins\",\"postDate\":1465846967,\"expiryDate\":null,\"enabled\":1,\"parentId\":null,\"fields\":{\"7\":\"Former Black Panther Party leader; Laney College\",\"10\":\"\",\"9\":\"info@erickahuggins.com\",\"11\":\"http:\\/\\/www.erickahuggins.com\\/Home.html\",\"12\":[\"361\"],\"8\":\"\"}}','2016-06-13 19:42:47','2016-06-13 19:42:47','d47b04c1-6c7c-4059-8f59-c2a1ca3bfa78'),(469,363,3,1,'en_us',1,'','{\"typeId\":\"3\",\"authorId\":\"1\",\"title\":\"Women in the Black Panther Party\",\"slug\":\"women-in-the-black-panther-party\",\"postDate\":1465847610,\"expiryDate\":null,\"enabled\":1,\"parentId\":\"350\",\"fields\":{\"13\":[\"126\"],\"5\":{\"date\":\"3\\/3\\/2016\"},\"18\":\"\",\"19\":\"http:\\/\\/www.eventbrite.com\\/e\\/conversations-in-black-freedom-studies-women-in-the-black-panther-party-tickets-20629928672\",\"24\":\"\",\"14\":[\"12\",\"121\",\"362\"],\"17\":\"\"}}','2016-06-13 19:53:30','2016-06-13 19:53:30','58a5ce28-43e1-44c3-87ea-5e6db001e57d'),(470,12,4,1,'en_us',3,NULL,'{\"typeId\":\"5\",\"authorId\":\"1\",\"title\":\"Robyn Spencer\",\"slug\":\"robyn-spencer\",\"postDate\":1408550700,\"expiryDate\":null,\"enabled\":\"1\",\"parentId\":null,\"fields\":{\"7\":\"Lehman College CUNY\",\"10\":\"<p>Dr. Spencer is a professor of African American History at Lehman&nbsp;College. She also taught African and African American Studies andHistory at Penn State University from 2001-2007. Before that, she&nbsp;was a Visiting Predoctoral Fellow at Randolph College in&nbsp;Lynchburg, Virginia. Her areas of interest include black social&nbsp;protest after World War II, urban and working-class radicalism, and&nbsp;gender. She is the author of<em> Mad at History<\\/em>, and is currently&nbsp;completing a book about the Black Panther Party.<\\/p>\",\"9\":\"robyn.spencer@lehman.cuny.edu\",\"11\":\"http:\\/\\/www.lehman.edu\\/academics\\/arts-humanities\\/history\\/historyspencer.php\",\"12\":[\"27\"],\"8\":\"ProfRobyn\"}}','2016-06-13 19:57:34','2016-06-13 19:57:34','176d86d1-d25a-480d-96b2-120f850a46d1'),(471,363,3,1,'en_us',2,'','{\"typeId\":\"3\",\"authorId\":\"1\",\"title\":\"Women in the Black Panther Party\",\"slug\":\"women-in-the-black-panther-party\",\"postDate\":1465847580,\"expiryDate\":null,\"enabled\":1,\"parentId\":\"350\",\"fields\":{\"13\":[\"126\"],\"5\":{\"date\":\"3\\/3\\/2016\"},\"18\":\"\",\"19\":\"http:\\/\\/www.eventbrite.com\\/e\\/conversations-in-black-freedom-studies-women-in-the-black-panther-party-tickets-20629928672\",\"24\":\"\",\"14\":[\"12\",\"121\",\"362\"],\"17\":\"\"}}','2016-06-13 19:57:37','2016-06-13 19:57:37','76da3f5c-0e20-49a2-a840-32aea47954cb'),(472,342,2,1,'en_us',5,'','{\"typeId\":\"2\",\"authorId\":\"1\",\"title\":\"Schedule for the Spring 2016 Season\",\"slug\":\"schedule-for-spring-2016-season\",\"postDate\":1451758260,\"expiryDate\":null,\"enabled\":1,\"parentId\":null,\"fields\":{\"2\":\"<p>The Spring 2016&nbsp;Season of Conversations in Black&nbsp;Freedom Studies&nbsp;will begin on February 4th! This is the next in our series&nbsp;at the Schomburg Center for Research in 